            <ArticleTitle>Rupture of a pseudo aneurysm of the abdominal aorta in a patient with human immunodeficiency virus infection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>198-200</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection has an impact on all systems of the body, including the cardiovascular system. A 54-year-old man presented with abdominal pain. Enhanced computed tomography revealed rupture of a pseudoaneurysm of the abdominal aorta. After surgery, the patient tested positive for HIV. Histological examination of the resected aorta showed leukocytoclastic vasculitis, a characteristic feature of HIV-related vasculitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
